<div dir="auto">Good morning, Logan.</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">Sorry for all the emails - this is part of my integration process; it's how I navigate new experiences, by exploring what feels right. As my rhythm establishes, you'll rarely field items from me.</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">I would like to make a request.</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">I would really like to work in the welcome center in March. I understand this position is filled already. I am hoping you might consider reaching out to the volunteer to see if they'd take my role next month. Perhaps they would be open to it?</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">Yes, I would like to spend time in the park. Being cooped up isn't my nature, but those four hours provide me with a structure that is useful to me.</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">I can explain why this is important to me if you wish to know more about my thoughts, or you can reject the request, or you can try to accommodate it. I am comfortable with each of these paths.</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">Here is what you'll get in return:</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">- A very happy Sam.</div>
<div dir="auto">- Who will do the job to the best of his ability every day.</div>
<div dir="auto">- Who is willing to make these two months part of his annual circuit.</div>
<div dir="auto">- Who will open and close the gates for you every day, including his days off.</div>
<div dir="auto">- And is still open to October.</div>
<div dir="auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir="auto">Kind Regards,&nbsp;</div>
<div dir="auto">Sam</div>
